  "section_notes": "The final rules are strict on incident reporting (24h, all incidents, prompt customer notice) and mandatory recall at 8/100k, but allow a 6-year retrofit and 36-month suppression phase-in. S2 sets a 55°C/5% test limit but does not stop sales for exceedance and provides per-model results to customers, not the public. S5 mandates recall for models above 8/100k, notably affecting Halcyon's Ember 8, but does not automatically ban sales."
